**Given:**

In-radius of an equilateral triangle = 3 cm

Concept used:

In-radius of equilateral triangle = (side)/(2sqrt{3)} 

The perimeter of the equilateral triangle = 3 × side

**Calculation:**

In-radius of equilateral triangle = (side)/(2sqrt{3)} 

⇒ 3=(side)/(2sqrt{3)} 

⇒ Side = 6√3 cm

Perimeter of equilateral triangle = 3 × side = 3 × 6√3 = 18√3 cm

**∴ The correct answer is 18√3 cm.**

